                <pb facs="0665" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg567"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram received in
                    cipher.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic">January 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[Mr. Choate states that Messrs. Flint, Eddy &amp; Co., in a letter dated New
                    York, January 9, informed their representative in London that Bridler &amp; Co.
                    reported that after considerable delay all goods shipped by the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maria</hi> for Delagoa Bay had been delivered.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
